ce26840610a2425eb7f17fb57fd","event_uuid":"ba1bb595-25ca-40a0-80f9-6c6e0317de5d","position":{"commit_sha":"d7c94bfb4bfb99643ebcbc4f774c1c9f499373d4","position":"1787063094881463001-ba1bb595-25ca-40a0-80f9-6c6e0317de5d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"900fde3ca892f3bdc8a552bf7b6494d084e86149ef2b629e2e27290f1c3c3a0f","event_uuid":"8e445a60-d124-4741-a0c1-9eba506edc72","position":{"commit_sha":"30e6917d531df4e144abf3974601597e409b1ce3","position":"1787063113413855001-8e445a60-d124-4741-a0c1-9eba506edc72"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9653bfc550ed57858e7704d82cbc521c7019845b07efc2bf4956b6aa6cf78b64","event_uuid":"1ca5c2fa-dd3f-4ecb-aa81-6c713fd14bde","position":{"commit_sha":"6aeb43195bbc70f2053b58f4b6a10c5aa9a8a1e1","position":"1787063145932873001-1ca5c2fa-dd3f-4ecb-aa81-6c713fd14bde"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed RCA (before repair):\n\nThe heartbeat window contains two mechanisms. The persistent outage is a code defect: commit 557f8c16e35 introduced `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py:39` with unconditional module-scope `from pydantic import SecretStr`, and commit 40b8ac8295 activated that module on every live pass through `reconcile.py:94-96`. The bridge deliberately runs `pip install .` without `[agents]` (`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, Install rebar), while `pyproject.toml:61-66` and `docs/config.md:44-52` define the engine/reconciler as stdlib-only and place pydantic only in the optional agents extra. Therefore three consecutive scheduled passes (32132211322, 32137600442, 32143243238) stop before config/network with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named pydantic`.\n\nDiscriminating proof: a fresh local no-extras install had `find_spec(\"pydantic\") is None` and reproduced the exact runtime.py:39 traceback. Installing only pydantic in that same venv made the runtime import succeed. Historical dynamic A/B probes with pydantic absent showed normal reconcile loading succeeds at 0f7461d243 (last-success head) and at 557f8c16e35 (runtime exists but is not activated), then fails at 40b8ac8295 at reconcile.py:94 -> runtime.py:39. This rules out Jira credentials, runner failure, packaging-path corruption, and a Pydantic API/version mismatch. Legitimacy: defect; it directly violates the cited stdlib-only reconciler contract and the workflow contract that reconcile needs no agents extra.\n\nThe first failed hour, run 32127284997 at head 4c3e5970e6, is separate: ACLI returned logical FAILURE editing REB-3162 (`Issue does not exist or you do not have permission`). A read-only `acli jira workitem view REB-3162` still returns the same visibility error. That environmental/shared-Jira mechanism is already tracked on open parentless bug `dutiable-shaded-honeyeater`; further confirmation would mutate Jira and remains awaiting explicit authorization. It does not explain the following three Pydantic failures.\n\nRepair target for this ticket: restore the stdlib-only runtime while preserving StaticAuth credential masking/reveal behavior, and add a clean-core bridge/runtime oracle so this contract cannot pass CI unexercised.","timestamp":1787062818989473001}],"created_at":1787062307468587260,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nThe Reconciler Heartbeat Canary detected a persistent bridge outage. Three consecutive scheduled passes fail before config or network because the stdlib-only reconciler runtime imports optional `pydantic` at module scope. A separate preceding REB-3162 visibility failure remains tracked on `dutiable-shaded-honeyeater`.\n\n## Proven root cause\nCommit 557f8c16e35 introduced `runtime.py` with `from pydantic import SecretStr`; 40b8ac8295 eagerly loads that runtime from every pass. The bridge installs `.` with no extras, while `pyproject.toml` and `docs/config.md` require the engine/reconciler to remain stdlib-only and place Pydantic only in `[agents]`. Clean-venv, dependency-perturbation, and historical A/B runtime probes confirm this exact activation edge.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Replace the Pydantic SecretStr dependency in `runtime.py` with a frozen stdlib credential carrier. Preserve credential hiding from repr/equality/hash, exact reveal at adapter authentication, and accurate presence checks.\n- Strengthen the existing clean-runtime subprocess oracle in `tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py` to load the real reconciler runtime while Pydantic is explicitly unavailable.\n- Prove RED before repair, GREEN after a held-out fix, then RED again under the exact module-scope Pydantic mutation.\n- Sweep the reconciler engine for other module-scope optional imports and disposition every confirmed sibling.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py -q` for the clean-runtime subprocess oracle.\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py -q` for credential and runtime behavior.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n- Build/install `.` in a fresh no-extras venv and import the packaged `rebar_reconciler.runtime` to replicate the original report.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py -q` executes the real reconciler runtime with Pydantic unavailable.\n- [ ] The clean-runtime subprocess imports no optional agents dependency.\n- [ ] Operation-binding tests prove credentials are absent from repr/equality/hash.\n- [ ] Operation-binding tests prove `reveal()` returns the exact credential.\n- [ ] The oracle is observed RED before repair.\n- [ ] The oracle is observed GREEN after repair.\n- [ ] Reintroducing the exact Pydantic import returns the oracle to RED.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] A fresh no-extras install imports the packaged reconciler runtime successfully.\n- [ ] The sibling sweep and dispositions are recorded on this ticket.","detected_by":"heartbeat-canary","env_id":"69d1248e-8618-44e1-ac4f-a94084ac0d61","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py","reason":"Remove the optional Pydantic import while preserving credential masking and reveal semantics."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py","reason":"Exercise the real reconciler runtime in a subprocess with Pydantic unavailable so Verified catches recurrence."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1e005609-475b-486d-85bd-2d7b9a329779","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["heartbeat-alert"],"ticket_id":"eab8-2009-2c59-46c7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"[heartbeat-canary] reconcile-bridge stale (2026-08-18T13:36:25Z) — no success within 4h","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dd9